--- body ---
## Context

`BASH_ENV=~/.claude/scripts/bash-env.sh` is sourced at the startup of every
non-interactive bash. Its credential loading uses two ordinary command forms —
`source "$_be_keyfile"` under `set -a` (l. 437) and `export "$_be_dst=$_be_val"`
(l. 465). Under `xtrace` bash prints both with the values already expanded, so a
plain `bash -x script.sh` writes live credentials to stderr.

Measured on the live environment 2026-09-16 (`bash -x -c ':'`, names only, values
never displayed): six variables exposed — `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`,
`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `HAL_ID`, `HAL_PASSWORD`, `KEYS`. A first pass with a
`length >= 16` filter reported five and silently dropped `HAL_PASSWORD`; the
filter was the defect, not the exposure.

The file already carries two `case "$-"` guards (l. 300, l. 355) but both guard
noglob (`-f`) only. There is no xtrace guard.

This is NOT the case `rules/coding-bash.md` § "Unsetting a variable in the parent
does not unset it in the child" already covers. That section's remedy
(`export BASH_ENV=`, or `env -i … bash -c`) makes a child you chose to isolate
hermetic, and is enforced across `tests/*.sh` by
`tests/test_bash_tests_are_hermetic.sh` (0359, green). It does not cover an
ordinary `bash -x script.sh` where the loader MUST run — the script needs the
keys — but must not be traced. The two remedies are complementary.

Does not reduce residency: the keys stay in the environment of every child, and
in `/proc/<pid>/environ`. On-demand loading is a separate question (no
`apiKeyHelper` is configured; consumers read `os.environ`).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `bash-env.sh` saves `xtrace` state, disables it before any credential
      handling, and restores the caller's setting at the end
- [ ] `tests/test_bash_env_xtrace_silent.sh` verifies it with a FAKE SENTINEL
      loader, never a real key, per `coding-bash.md` l. 170
- [ ] The test carries a firing positive control: the unguarded loader leaks the
      sentinel, so a later zero is measured and not blind
- [ ] Both export paths still export, and `xtrace` resumes for the calling script
- [ ] The test spawns hermetically (`env -i HOME=… BASH_ENV=…`), so
      `test_bash_tests_are_hermetic.sh` stays green
- [ ] `make check` passes
